-- title:
--   (A.59)–(A.63), OA pp.35–36 — the lower bound $\gamma$ under sublinear workload growth
-- statement:
--   Let $(f,B,\gamma)$ solve (13) and let $(W,I,E,a,S)$ be feasible for the EWF (10) with
--   $$\liminf_{t\to\infty}\frac{\mathbf E[W(t)]}{t}=0.$$
--   Then
--   $$\limsup_{t\to\infty}\frac1t\,\mathbf E\Big[\sum_ib_i\int_0^t(a_i(s)-S_i)^+\,ds+c_k\mu_kE(t)\Big]\ge\gamma.$$
--   Together with (A.45)–(A.47) this is the lower half of the optimality proof.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: (10f): a(·,W(·)) is 𝔽-adapted → progressive measurability, and integrable paths (aᵢ − Sᵢ)⁺ on every [0,t]; reason: the paper integrates these paths in (10a)–(10b) and applies Tonelli in (A.47), which needs both
--   - encoding: a(t,W(t,ω),ω) → one process a t ω; reason: the allocation is used only along the path
--   - encoding: real-valued expectations in (10a) → ℝ≥0∞ with lower integrals; reason: the integrands are nonnegative and an infinite expectation stays infinite
--   - generalization: Σ := Σᵢ αᵢλᵢ(1+σᵢ²)/μᵢ² (p.15) → Σ > 0 a free parameter; reason: every statement depends on Σ only through Σ > 0; the source value is one such Σ
--   - encoding: SKU set {1,…,I}, indices j, k → Fin n with n ≥ 1; bjμj/λj and ckμk as minima; reason: only the values of the minima enter the statements
--   - encoding: f ∈ C₂ with domain ℝ₊ → f : ℝ → ℝ, C² on ℝ, with (13) imposed for w ≥ 0; reason: a C² function on [0,∞) extends to ℝ, so no solution is lost
--   - generalization: 𝔽 generated by (Xᵢ) → any filtration for which X is a Brownian motion; reason: the natural filtration is one such filtration
-- source:
--   Özkan and van Houtum, Joint Inventory and Scheduling Control in a Repair Facility, SSRN 3784144 (2023), (A.59)–(A.63), OA pp.35–36

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_RepairSched_Model_IsBellman
import Definitions.Def_RepairSched_Model_backorderRatio
import Definitions.Def_RepairSched_Model_IsFeasible
import Definitions.Def_RepairSched_Model_avgBOE
import Definitions.Def_AtaBarjesteh23_Workload_DriftBM

open MeasureTheory Filter

namespace RepairSched

/-- **(A.59)–(A.63): the lower bound `γ` when the mean workload grows sublinearly.**
Özkan and van Houtum, *Joint Inventory and Scheduling Control in a Repair Facility*, SSRN 3784144 (2023), (A.59)–(A.63), OA pp.35–36 (PDF pp.75–76).

Let `(f, B, γ)` satisfy (13), let `X` be a Brownian motion with drift `0` and variance `Σ` for
`𝔽`, and let `(W, I, E, a, S)` be feasible for the EWF (10) with `liminf_{t→∞} E[W(t)]/t = 0`. Then
`limsup_{t→∞} (1/t) E[Σᵢ bᵢ ∫₀ᵗ (aᵢ(s,W(s)) − Sᵢ)⁺ ds + ckμkE(t)] ≥ γ`. -/
theorem equation_A_63 {n : ℕ} [NeZero n] (M : Model n) (S : Fin n → ℝ)
    (hEm : M.emergencyRate < M.backorderRatio) (f : ℝ → ℝ) (B γ : ℝ)
    (hBell : M.IsBellman S f B γ) {Ω : Type*} [mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω] (𝔽 : Filtration ℝ mΩ)
    (P : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure P] (X W I E : ℝ → Ω → ℝ) (a : ℝ → Ω → Fin n → ℝ)
    (hX : AtaBarjesteh23.Workload.IsDriftBM 𝔽 P X 0 (Real.sqrt M.Sigma))
    (hfeas : M.IsFeasible 𝔽 X S W I E a)
    (hlim : liminf (fun t : ℝ => (∫⁻ ω, ENNReal.ofReal (W t ω) ∂P) / ENNReal.ofReal t) atTop = 0) :
    ENNReal.ofReal γ ≤ limsup (M.avgBOE P S E a) atTop := by sorry

end RepairSched
